Good morning,

We are instructed to notify a fire loss on behalf of our client Fairmount Textile Mills Holdings, Inc. The affected operating company is Piedmont Dye & Finish, LLC. Our reference is RK/MFG/2024/2210.

Policy number: CP-2210-55870
Insured name: Fairmount Textile Mills Holdings, Inc.
Date of loss: 13 August 2025
Loss location: 1180 Woodruff Industrial Road, Greenville, SC 29607
Cause: Fire - hydraulic fluid release onto a hot thermal oil line
Estimated loss: USD 30,500,000

Fire broke out on the second shift at a hydraulic hose on one of the jet dye
machines in Building 1B and spread into the overhead cable tray and the dust
collection ductwork. Sprinklers operated and the plant brigade held it; it was
out by 22:47. No injuries beyond two brigade members treated for smoke
inhalation and released.

The dye house is the plant bottleneck and there is no redundancy, so the
business interruption element is likely to exceed the property damage. Our
client is already sourcing outsourced dyeing capacity.

Notice is given within the 48-hour requirement. Nothing has been moved and the
fire marshal's hold is still in place.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * forensic engineer's report
  * stock loss schedule

Please confirm a claim reference and an adjuster today. Our client will be
requesting an advance payment within the next fortnight.

